<header><p class="st-kicker">emirate · Iberia</p><h1 class="st-title">Second Taifa of Silves</h1><p class="st-meta">1144 CE – 1150 CE (approx.) · capital Silves</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Silves under the rebel Ibn al-Mundhir, one of the Algarve leaders who rose with Ibn Qasi against the Almoravids in 1144.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>In 1144 Abu Muhammad ibn al-Mundhir, a local notable and disciple of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sufism">Sufi</a> leader <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-qasi">Ibn Qasi</a>, took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silves">Silves</a> during the uprising of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/muridun">Muridun</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almoravid-empire">Almoravids</a> and governed it as an independent lord.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Known only from brief chronicle references, Ibn al-Mundhir's rule was one of the short-lived regimes of the second <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/taifa">taifa</a> period. He first backed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-qasi">Ibn Qasi</a> of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/second-taifa-of-mertola">Second Taifa of Mértola</a>, then joined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sidray-ibn-wazir">Sidray ibn Wazir</a> of Beja against him.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Around 1150 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silves">Silves</a> accepted <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/almohad-caliphate">Almohad</a> authority. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-qasi">Ibn Qasi</a> was killed in the city in 1151. Silves was taken briefly by Sancho I of Portugal in 1189, lost again, and finally conquered by Portugal in 1242.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="emirate, 1144 CE – 1150 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M24 82 V62 Q24 40 50 34 Q76 40 76 62 V82 Z"/><path d="M50 34 V24"/><path d="M53 13 A6 6 0 1 0 53 25 A4.5 4.5 0 1 1 53 13"/><path d="M38 82 V66 Q44 58 50 66 V82"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">emirate</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Iberia</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:82.47%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1144 CE – 1150 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/12th-century">12th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>emirate</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>feudal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Silves</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Ibn al-Mundhir</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Sunni Islam</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Andalusi Arabic</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/portugal">Portugal</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Silves of Ibn al-Mundhir</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1147&amp;focus=second-taifa-of-silves" aria-label="Second Taifa of Silves on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="4469 839 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Second Taifa of Silves lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M4789 1095L4799 1289M4789 1095L4794 1282"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M4799 1289h0M4794 1282h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M4789 1095h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M4789 1095h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Silves. <a href="/atlas?year=1147&amp;focus=second-taifa-of-silves">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
